        "body": "This bugfix release allows autoscaling compute managers to start with the `--steal` flag, even when no existing registration is present on the server. This effectively allows permissive running of a compute manager by operators when they are confident no other manager with the same name is running, especially when the manager is running in environments where it may be killed without warning.\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* Set Python support window to 3.12, 3.13, 3.14 by @dotsdl in https://github.com/OpenFreeEnergy/alchemiscale/pull/523\r\n* Allow steal when registering an unregistered compute manager by @dotsdl in https://github.com/OpenFreeEnergy/alchemiscale/pull/525\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/OpenFreeEnergy/alchemiscale/compare/v0.8.0...v0.8.1",
